 "summary": "The weak Cauchy\u2013Riemann predicates have the full set of supporting lemmas (unfolding, open-set form, monotonicity, independence of the weak derivative, C\u00b9 comparison, a simp-normal constant-map lemma, linear closure), there is no compatibility layer, and the general linear-algebra criterion is in its canonical home. The earlier finding on the private `fderiv_conj_apply` is withdrawn: it only restates Mathlib's `ContinuousLinearEquiv.fderiv` for `conjCLE` in applied form, so publishing it would duplicate an existing Mathlib lemma under a new name, as the reuse review says.",
